      "prompt": "A biased spinner can only land on red or blue. The probability that it lands on red is x, and the probability that it lands on blue is 1 - x. Landing on blue is 5 times as likely as landing on red. The spinner is spun twice. Find the probability that both spins land on red.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "A biased spinner can only land on red or blue. The probability that it lands on red is x, and the probability that it lands on blue is 1 - x. Landing on blue is 5 times as likely as landing on red. Since the spinner can only land on red or blue, the two probabilities must sum to 1: x + 5x = 1.",
        "Solving this equation gives x = 1/6.",
        "Substituting back: P(red) = 1/6, P(blue) = 5/6.",
        "P(both spins land on red) = 1/6 × 1/6 = 1/36"
